WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.394 --> 00:00:02.065
(tango music)

00:00:02.065 --> 00:00:03.502
- Usually when people
first see the manikin

00:00:03.502 --> 00:00:05.859
they're kind of wondering, you know,
what does it do,

00:00:05.859 --> 00:00:07.960
I mean what's the purpose of it?

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:11.214
It has a mouth, it has
teeth, it has soft gums,

00:00:11.214 --> 00:00:12.667
it has a cheek.

00:00:12.667 --> 00:00:16.417
You can tell we got the
same haircut as well.

00:00:20.618 --> 00:00:21.680
My name is Philip Briales.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:25.054
I am the Director of Sales
for Columbia Dentoform.

00:00:25.054 --> 00:00:28.103
We supply dental manikins
to dental schools.

00:00:28.103 --> 00:00:29.970
What we basically supply
is their first patient

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:31.817
for them to train on before they actually

00:00:31.817 --> 00:00:33.857
move on to live patients.

00:00:33.857 --> 00:00:36.613
The company started in 1917

00:00:36.613 --> 00:00:41.262
so next year, Columbia
Dentoform will be 100 years old.

00:00:41.262 --> 00:00:44.867
The models, the manikins
are all assembled by hand.

00:00:44.867 --> 00:00:46.728
We sell well over a million teeth a year.

00:00:46.728 --> 00:00:49.373
(snapping)

00:00:49.373 --> 00:00:51.088
We make a variety of models.

00:00:51.088 --> 00:00:53.231
We provide models that
put tartar on the teeth.

00:00:53.231 --> 00:00:55.909
We make models that have
a variety of disease

00:00:55.909 --> 00:00:57.870
under the gums, on the gums.

00:00:57.870 --> 00:00:58.804
If they need to,

00:00:58.804 --> 00:01:02.039
they could do a root canal
on the dog and cat as well.

00:01:02.039 --> 00:01:05.158
We have models that have
absolutely no teeth at all

00:01:05.158 --> 00:01:07.760
so they can learn how to
do a complete denture.

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:09.904
(clicking)

00:01:09.904 --> 00:01:13.271
The reason why it actually looks this way,

00:01:13.271 --> 00:01:15.904
we really didn't want to put
any gender in the manikin

00:01:15.904 --> 00:01:17.751
and so this could be anybody.

00:01:17.751 --> 00:01:21.524
The design of it is based
on what an average human

00:01:21.524 --> 00:01:23.809
would look like as far as
the size of the head, the ears,

00:01:23.809 --> 00:01:26.560
the mouth opening, the
softness of the gum tissue.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:27.683
The only thing it doesn't simulate

00:01:27.683 --> 00:01:29.168
is maybe the bad breath,

00:01:29.168 --> 00:01:31.729
but other than that it's a great patient

00:01:31.729 --> 00:01:35.330
because it just cooperates with you.

00:01:35.330 --> 00:01:37.330
I've been with the company for 41 years.

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:39.239
I have no idea that I'd be working with

00:01:39.239 --> 00:01:42.801
dental manikins at all or all these teeth.

00:01:42.801 --> 00:01:45.520
My granddaughters think I
work for the tooth fairy

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:47.034
and so that really works out well

00:01:47.034 --> 00:01:48.773
because if their parent forget

00:01:48.773 --> 00:01:51.280
to put money under the pillow for a tooth,

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:52.897
they'll tell mom just talk to grandpa,

00:01:52.897 --> 00:01:55.064
he knows the tooth fairy.

